  "text": "## Project: Sri Vinayaka Group — Sleeper Bus, Logistics & Tours Website\nCase study page (share this): https://bineeshs.vercel.app/project?slug=sri-vinayaka-group\nLive website (share only if asked to see it): https://www.srivinayakagroup.com/\nSource repository: https://github.com/Bineesh627/SriVinayakaGroup\nTechnologies: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, SEO, Service Worker, llms.txt, Vercel\nSummary: A multi-page, SEO- and AI-search-optimised website for Sri Vinayaka Group covering Bangalore–Coorg AC sleeper buses, overnight parcel logistics and tour packages, built with HTML, CSS and JavaScript.\nQuick facts: Category: Transport & Tourism Website; Verticals: Sleeper Bus · Logistics · Tours; Region: Bangalore · Coorg · Mysore; Stack: HTML · CSS · JavaScript\nCase study details: Sri Vinayaka Group: Driven by Trust Sri Vinayaka Group is a South Indian transport enterprise running overnight AC sleeper buses between Bangalore and Coorg, express parcel logistics and holiday tours. I built a fast, mobile-friendly website that presents all three businesses under one trusted brand. Pages & Services - Sleeper bus page: daily overnight Bangalore ↔ Coorg service, fleet amenities, fixed departure times and the full list of boarding and dropping points. - Logistics page: guaranteed overnight parcel delivery with booking cut-off, cargo types handled and hub locations. - Tours page: weekend getaways, school and college trips and luxury coach charters, with photo galleries of the fleet and past trips. - About, Contact and a custom 404 page, with shared navbar and footer components. Discoverability - Page-level titles, descriptions, sitemap and robots rules. - llms.txt and llms.jsonl files so AI assistants can describe the business accurately. - Optimised WebP imagery across the fleet and tour galleries. Performance A service worker, cache headers and lightweight static pages keep load times low on mobile networks, where most customers browse.",
