  "keys": "AgriCrop AI — Smart Crop Recommendation & Analytics agricrop ai Python Django Scikit-Learn Random Forest Pandas NumPy SQLite JavaScript project",
  "text": "## Project: AgriCrop AI — Smart Crop Recommendation & Analytics\nCase study page (share this): https://bineeshs.vercel.app/project?slug=agricrop-ai\nSource repository: https://github.com/Bineesh627/agricrop_ai\nTechnologies: Python, Django, Scikit-Learn, Random Forest, Pandas, NumPy, SQLite, JavaScript\nSummary: A Django and scikit-learn web app that recommends the best crop from soil nutrients (N, P, K, pH) and climate (temperature, humidity, rainfall), with a crop library, prediction history and farmer/admin roles.\nQuick facts: Category: Agri-Tech ML Application; Model: Random Forest Classifier; Inputs: N · P · K · pH · Temp · Humidity · Rainfall; Users: Farmers · Administrators\nCase study details: AgriCrop AI: Know What to Grow Before You Plant AgriCrop AI helps farmers, advisors and researchers choose the most suitable crop for their land. It combines a trained machine-learning model with a practical crop knowledge base inside a Django web app. How It Works - The user enters soil nutrient levels ( Nitrogen, Phosphorus, Potassium ) and pH , plus temperature, humidity and rainfall . - Inputs are scaled and passed to a Random Forest classifier (an ensemble of 100 decision trees) trained on a crop-recommendation dataset. - The app returns the recommended crop with supporting agronomic guidance. Features - Crop library: ideal growing conditions, fertiliser split-dosing, water needs and harvest periods for cereals, pulses, fruits and cash crops, seeded from a structured catalogue. - Prediction history so logged-in users can review past recommendations. - Roles: Farmer and Administrator profiles; admins can retrain the model from within the app. - Feedback and support form to reach the administrators. - Seed scripts that populate the database with standard crop profiles. Tech Stack - Python, Django 4.2, SQLite - Scikit-Learn, Pandas, NumPy, Joblib - HTML, CSS, JavaScript and Font Awesome",
